WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
White House ceremonies break the news to the world of the epic feat of the atomic submarine Nautilus.

00:09.000 --> 00:14.000
President Eisenhower personally awards the Legion of Merit to her commander, W.R. Anderson,

00:14.000 --> 00:20.000
who skippered the 1,830-mile voyage from Pearl Harbor north, under the Arctic ice cap and the North Pole,

00:20.000 --> 00:22.000
into the waters of the Atlantic.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.000
It was only a claim for Commander Anderson, his ship and crew,

00:26.000 --> 00:39.000
who pioneered a seaway across the top of the world, a 6,000-mile shortcut from the Pacific to Europe.

00:39.000 --> 00:42.000
With the mighty Nautilus submerged for the 96-hour cruise,

00:42.000 --> 00:47.000
the voyage was a quiet one for the 116 crewmen and scientific observers.

00:47.000 --> 00:52.000
No emergencies, no encounters with fanciful sea monsters, a la Jules Verne.

00:52.000 --> 00:58.000
But always there was a sense of adventure as the Nautilus logged a cruise that will rank with man's first strides into space

00:58.000 --> 01:01.000
in the annals of 20th century achievement.

01:01.000 --> 01:22.000
Music.

